WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.323
Same quality every time needs a checklist, not memory.

00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:05.538
This lesson is about delivery checklist.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.015
Same quality every time.

00:00:07.015 --> 00:00:09.599
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:13.291
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.291 --> 00:00:18.829
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:22.891
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:26.952
Stay practical: write delivery checklist before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:30.239
Write a delivery checklist from kickoff to done.

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:32.463
Remember the objective: write delivery checklist.

00:00:32.463 --> 00:00:36.542
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:40.992
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:45.071
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:45.071 --> 00:00:49.521
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:49.521 --> 00:00:52.117
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:53.600
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.004
